    "title": "Here’s Exciting News For Fans Wanting A ‘Scarpetta’ Season 2",
    "text": "Scarpetta, Nicole Kidman’s new crime mystery series based on Patricia Cornwell’s classic literary character, is new on streaming and there’s more on the way.Directed by David Gordon Green, Scarpetta Season 1 premiered on Wednesday on Prime Video with all eight episodes dropping at the same time. The official synopsis for the series reads, “With skilled hands and an unnerving eye, this unrelenting medical examiner is determined to serve as the voice of the victims, unmask a serial killer, and prove that her career-making case from 28 years prior isn't also her undoing.MORE FROM FORBESNicole Kidman’s ‘Scarpetta’ Is Now Streaming - How To WatchBy Tim Lammers“Set against the backdrop of modern forensic investigation, the series delves beyond the crime scene to explore the psychological complexities of both perpetrators and investigators, creating a multi-layered thriller that examines the toll of pursuing justice at all costs.”Scarpetta also stars Jamie Lee Curtis, Bobby Cannavale, Simon Baker, Ariana DeBose, Rosy McEwen, Amanda Righetti, Jake Cannavale and Hunter Parrish.While most series need to wait for viewership numbers to determine if it will return for another season, Scarpetta already has its immediate future carved out. In a Sept. 28, 2024, press release, Prime Video, which is streaming Scarpetta, announced that it had ordered two seasons of the series.MORE FROM FORBESOscars 2026 Predictions: Who Will Win Best Picture, Best Actor And MoreBy Tim LammersAn announcement of when viewers can expect Scarpetta Season 2 to begin streaming on Prime Video is pending. TV Insider reported on March 4 that Scarpetta Season 2 was expected to go into production on March 9.Patricia Cornwell Is Thrilled Over Nicole Kidman And Jamie Lee Curtis’ Involvement In 'Scarpetta'In a statement in the September 2024 press release announcing that Scarpetta was going to become a series, author Patricia Cornwell expressed her excitement about working with Nicole Kidman and Jamie Lee Curtis.“I’m beyond excited that this is finally happening. This will be great fun for all, and I’m grateful for the immense talent that the show is drawing, Cornwell said in a statement in the September 2024 press release. “I’ve always been a huge fan of Jamie Lee Curtis and Nicole Kidman. Their wanting to do this is humbling and simply awesome.\"MORE FROM FORBES‘Project Hail Mary’ Rotten Tomatoes Reviews: Ryan Gosling Film Fires On All BurnersBy Tim LammersKidman expressed in an Instagram post on Wednesday how grateful she was to have the opportunity to star in the title role in Scarpetta.“Thank you, Patricia Cornwell for choosing me to play your Dr. Kay Scarpetta … I love her - hope you all do too,” Kidman said in the post, which is accompanied by a photo of her and Cornwell on the set of the series.All eight episodes of Scarpetta are streaming on Prime Video.MORE FROM FORBESBruce Campbell On His Decision To Be Less Involved In ‘Evil Dead’ FilmsBy Tim Lammers",
